{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1074619-invention-system-in-trinity-continuum","id":1074619,"title":"Invention system in Trinity Continuum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-07T06:21:51-07:00","id":1074619,"title":"Invention system in Trinity Continuum?","content":"hi folks, <br /> <br /> I've been thinking about this question literally all night, and I wanted to pop back onto the forums (it's been a while) to ask it. <br /> <br /> Are we going to be getting a system in Trinity continuum that allows us to make Powered items? I.e. Captain America's shield, Iron Man's Armor, Black Panther's suit? <br /> <br /> especially for Daredevils, this could be really important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T11:39:13-07:00","id":1074767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HammerofHeaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1074619-invention-system-in-trinity-continuum#post1074619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hi folks,<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about this question literally all night, and I wanted to pop back onto the forums (it's been a while) to ask it.<br /> <br /> Are we going to be getting a system in Trinity continuum that allows us to make Powered items? I.e. Captain America's shield, Iron Man's Armor, Black Panther's suit?<br /> <br /> especially for Daredevils, this could be really important.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I remember, yes. There's going to be an option to play a super genius, and rules to create supertechnology, whether it be gadgets, weapons, or powered armors. However, I'm not sure if that is only going to be available in aberrant, or the whole line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T13:37:49-07:00","id":1074853,"title":"","content":"And of course I can't find it but I thought word on the street was there'd be a comprehensive guide to gadgets (oh, now we CAN be Iron Man...) in the Aberrant game. Of course I can't find it but it's a great idea to introduce it early. Although I don't think it was the right setting to get all Gundam-y, I kinda liked that the good guys in Aeon tried to even the odds with VARGs. You'd guess that if psions need a boost in power that daredevils really would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T18:33:48-07:00","id":1074939,"title":"","content":"Yes, the <b>Trinity Continuum</b> rulebook has rules for Super-Science.Lauren Roy wrote the section, which includes Advanced Science, Inspired Science, and Powered Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T21:45:11-07:00","id":1075365,"title":"","content":"Woooooo! I fell like we are looking at a Daredevil/Psion/Nova split for science in the above, but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T21:57:17-07:00","id":1075370,"title":"","content":"I noticed that in Adventure! 1ed, there are robots in the antagonist section and a few of the villain NPCs are said to be able to invent such creations... but going through the super-science chapter leaves me wondering how they do this. It seems that while they are able to make robots and such, the PCs are not allowed to, given the rules presented.<br /> <br /> \u200bAm I missing something?<br /> <br /> \u200bHopefully this will be addressed in the new edition. True, players shouldn't be creating armies of minions to take over the world... but a robotic companion (like S.K.E.E.T.S. for Booster Gold) should be somewhat possible, yes? A clockwork parrot that can record what it hears and repeat it back... a robotic dog with a powerful ray projector in its nose and an almost encyclopedia of knowledge stored in its artificial brain... such things wouldn't be too overpowering for a player... would they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T05:18:57-07:00","id":1075439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1074619-invention-system-in-trinity-continuum?p=1075365#post1075365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woooooo! I fell like we are looking at a Daredevil/Psion/Nova split for science in the above, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Advanced Science is a creation which is a decade or so ahead of its time, but otherwise mundane.<br /> <br /> Inspired Science is a creation which can only be created by someone Inspired, but is usable by anyone. Once that freeze ray's been constructed, anyone can steal it and press the trigger.<br /> <br /> Powered Science is a creation which can only be created and used by someone Inspired, as it's powered by the user's Source: Psi or Quantum, most likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:15:28-07:00","id":1075599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1074619-invention-system-in-trinity-continuum?p=1075370#post1075370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHopefully this will be addressed in the new edition. True, players shouldn't be creating armies of minions to take over the world... but a robotic companion (like S.K.E.E.T.S. for Booster Gold) should be somewhat possible, yes? A clockwork parrot that can record what it hears and repeat it back... a robotic dog with a powerful ray projector in its nose and an almost encyclopedia of knowledge stored in its artificial brain... such things wouldn't be too overpowering for a player... would they?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would still need some adjustment. If you can just build a robot to do something for you, then why bother learning how to do it? If you have to know how to do it to build the robot, why build the robot instead of doing it yourself?<br /> <br /> Plus no, we don't want players just building robots to go play the game for them, although I hope most players would be smart enough to realize how against the interests of their personal enjoyment that is.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T15:17:40-07:00","id":1075601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1074619-invention-system-in-trinity-continuum?p=1075439#post1075439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> Advanced Science is a creation which is a decade or so ahead of its time, but otherwise mundane.<br /> <br /> Inspired Science is a creation which can only be created by someone Inspired, but is usable by anyone. Once that freeze ray's been constructed, anyone can steal it and press the trigger.<br /> <br /> Powered Science is a creation which can only be created and used by someone Inspired, as it's powered by the user's Source: Psi or Quantum, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that Advanced Science relative to the particular time period, or is it relative to real world tech?<br /> <br /> Edit: Really, now I'm slightly curious how this will transfer over to Aegis, and if it's going to be the kind of setting where creating anachronistic technology would be encouraged or discouraged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T18:50:32-07:00","id":1075668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1074619-invention-system-in-trinity-continuum?p=1075599#post1075599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would still need some adjustment. If you can just build a robot to do something for you, then why bother learning how to do it? If you have to know how to do it to build the robot, why build the robot instead of doing it yourself?<br /> <br /> Plus no, we don't want players just building robots to go play the game for them, although I hope most players would be smart enough to realize how against the interests of their personal enjoyment that is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWasn't suggesting that a player create a robot to adventure for them... but rather to do things they can not... at least not in a timely manner. A physically weak inventor might create a strong robot to protect her. A inventor that isn't particularly stealthy might create a menagerie of robotic animals to go places he can't... and gather information that he can't (the clockwork parrot that records and replay all it hears).<br /> <br /> \u200bWho says that an inventor has to know what a robot can do before he can make it? Does that mean that an inventor has to be strong to make a brute of a robot? Has to be stealthy to create a robot that can sneak around to gather attention? To know how to throw fireballs to build a flame projector into a robot?<br /> <br /> \u200bBe the reasoning you provide... why build anything? Isn't building a suit of armor preventing the inventor from improving their Stamina? Wouldn't building a better gun mean you don't need to learn to shoot better?<br /> <br /> \u200bJust because someone can potentially do something themselves... or learn a skill themselves, doesn't mean that they have the time or desire to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:10:59-07:00","id":1076136,"title":"","content":"In the case of armor and Stamina, that's a matter that the inventor is building something because she CAN'T do it, barring unusual circumstances; armor might stop bullets but skin won't without some kind of miraculous power coming into play. In that sense it answers my question nicely: Why bother to learn to do it if you can build something to do it for you? Because you can't learn to do it-again, barring unusual circumstances.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:57:25-07:00","id":1076296,"title":"","content":"Because a character shouldn't have to learn everything or master everything.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I want to play a physically weak character who has created a brute of a robot as a protector for herself... something to run interference with a mob boss's mooks while I disarm a bomb... or help evacuate the senator's daughter that was kidnapped... then I should be allowed to. She is not the kind of character that will take on physically stronger opponents herself... as she is intelligent to know she isn't strong enough... may never be strong enough to do so. So she used what she is good at... her mind... to build something that can handle the heavy lifting for her... to fight the Extras that she needs to get past... to protect her from the danger she faces... because she can't do those things herself... and shouldn't be expected to do so.<br /> <br /> \u200bA mental primary character should do what they do best... think their way out of a problem... not have to learn physical skills to deal with the problem as a Physical Primary character is likely to do. Inventors should be allowed to create the inventions they want... not the ones &quot;You&quot; deem appropriate.<br /> <br /> \u200bHow is having an robotic companion any different than an animal companion? Both provide a character with an NPC that gives them abilities they don't possess. Yes, a robot may be tougher than an animal... and may even have abilities that an animal won't... but it won't &quot;heal&quot; when it takes damage unless repaired... and unlike an animal... a robot's unusual abilities may fail... and are likely to be much heavier than an animal (requiring a means of transportation that can carry them... or even having to be careful what kind of terrain it is on... a stealthy robotic cat is nor going to be able to cross a clothesline like a trained cat might be able to use). The capture and reprograming of a Robotic Companion is also something to consider... especially if an Inventor is forced to leave their companion behind due to excessive damage crippling it.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust like any other NPC (ally, animal companion, contact)... a robotic companion can be a source of much adventure for a character... both building it, using it, maintaining it, loosing it (temporarily). How is the inventor of such a wondrous creation any different than the inventor of a dozen or more inventions that do much the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:47:24-07:00","id":1076339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1074619-invention-system-in-trinity-continuum?p=1075601#post1075601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that Advanced Science relative to the particular time period, or is it relative to real world tech?<br /> <br /> Edit: Really, now I'm slightly curious how this will transfer over to Aegis, and if it's going to be the kind of setting where creating anachronistic technology would be encouraged or discouraged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hephaestus and Daedalus suggest it could be a valid part of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T00:33:58-07:00","id":1076351,"title":"","content":"Wikipedia, on Daedalus: &quot;Pliny's Natural History (7.198) he is credited with inventing carpentry. Pausanias, in travelling around Greece, attributed to Daedalus numerous archaic wooden cult figures that impressed him: 'All the works of this artist, though somewhat uncouth to look at, nevertheless have a touch of the divine in them.' It is said he first conceived masts and sails for ships for the navy of Minos. He is said to have carved statues so well they looked as if alive; even possessing self-motion. They would have escaped if not for the chain that bound them to the wall.&quot; He's also said to have built the Labyrinth for Minos.<br /> <br /> Less canonically, you could also look at his presentation in God of War: the Labyrinth he build was considerably more complex.<br /> <br /> And then there's stuff like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antikythera_mechanism\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:20:21-07:00","id":1077210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1074619-invention-system-in-trinity-continuum?p=1075439#post1075439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> Advanced Science is a creation which is a decade or so ahead of its time, but otherwise mundane.<br /> <br /> Inspired Science is a creation which can only be created by someone Inspired, but is usable by anyone. Once that freeze ray's been constructed, anyone can steal it and press the trigger.<br /> <br /> Powered Science is a creation which can only be created and used by someone Inspired, as it's powered by the user's Source: Psi or Quantum, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for instance, (and correct me if I'm wrong) to avoid using weapons or computers, a cure for cancer with expected medical side affects would be Advanced Science, an actual cure all would be (attmidedly high end) Inspired Science, and a treatment that made you immune to disease and have fast healing for life would be Powered Science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:50:17-07:00","id":1077449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1074619-invention-system-in-trinity-continuum?p=1076351#post1076351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Less canonically, you could also look at his presentation in God of War: the Labyrinth he build was considerably more complex.<br /> <br /> And then there's stuff like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antikythera_mechanism\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or for pure ridiculousness, Mechanicles from the Aladdin animated cartoon series.<br /> <br /> I thought it might cool, but I wasn't sure if that is what you were going for. It's good to see all have Science! at least partially in their theme; it makes a good counterpoint to the WoD/CoD games.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"